  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "909359ea-2e71-4762-98fd-3a07adc77e92"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "gives the vertices of the subgraph ",
 StyleBox["h", "TI"],
 " whose edges in ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 " are all edges of ",
 StyleBox["h", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"422a7471-dc81-4b60-bc75-11150acf6fcf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Definition: the interior of a set ",
 StyleBox["S", "TI"],
 " of vertices of ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 " is int ",
 StyleBox["S", "TI"],
 " = {",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " \[Element] ",
 StyleBox["S", "TI"],
 " : every neighbour of ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " lies in ",
 StyleBox["S", "TI"],
 "}, the vertices whose closed ball of radius 1 lies in ",
 StyleBox["S", "TI"],
 ". It is ",
 StyleBox["S", "TI"],
 " less its ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["GraphBoundary"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/GraphBoundary", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "3b62a6b7-3614-4498-a39a-cc6e81e51090"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"62354905-9326-4ac6-bf75-a681d27215a5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The interior of an intersection is the intersection of the interiors, and a \
smaller set has a smaller interior. The interior of the ball of radius ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " contains the ball of radius ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " \[Minus] 1, and equals it where the graph goes on beyond the ball."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b1a60406-3d32-4d52-8df9-f930723e2be0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A subgraph ",
 StyleBox["h", "TI"],
 " is read with its own edges: a vertex of ",
 StyleBox["h", "TI"],
 " is interior when every edge of ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 " at it is an edge of ",
 StyleBox["h", "TI"],
 ". For an induced subgraph the two readings agree; a path has no interior."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"75ad2dc8-be5d-4122-bc6b-859180ee9c3f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraInterior"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraInterior", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "9c6f847a-f00a-4847-914f-c80f6d671d0c"],
 " with its default method is the interior of the vertex set, sorted; it \
reads a subgraph by its vertices. It is the interior of a closure space, not \
of a topology: taking the interior again shrinks the set again, while the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["TopologicalInterior"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/TopologicalInterior", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "3e65e8af-d61a-4f90-8780-62c9dfbde512"],
 " of the ball topology stays put."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"8e936449-592e-4790-80bf-920666fe4360"]
}, Open  ]],

